  <section class="content-section reveal">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 lg:px-6">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Real-world impact</p>
      <h2 class="section-title mb-12">Sector scenarios & case studies</h2>
      <div class="reveal grid-2">
        <div class="prose-content">
          <p>A Gulf-region airbase required secure connectivity across multiple classified network domains with strict air-gap enforcement between operational, intelligence, and logistics systems. MEAICON deployed capture-resistant edge compute nodes at each network boundary, enabling cross-domain data transfer through hardware-enforced guards while maintaining physical separation. The platform operated on grid-independent power for extended periods, and geo-fence policies automatically restricted node functionality if equipment was moved beyond authorised perimeters.</p>
          <p>A North African defence ministry engaged MEAICON to segment a sprawling classified network spanning dozens of facilities into discrete security zones. Each zone received sovereign edge compute with hardware-rooted trust chains, ensuring that compromise of one zone could not propagate laterally. Remote zeroization capabilities allowed central command to irreversibly purge any node within seconds, and post-quantum-ready cryptography protected long-term intelligence archives against future decryption threats.</p>
          <p>For an East African border security programme, MEAICON architected a C5ISR data fusion platform that aggregated sensor feeds from ground radar, aerial surveillance, and coastal AIS into a single situational picture. Edge nodes processed and correlated telemetry locally, reducing satellite bandwidth dependency by filtering noise at the source. The platform maintained operational integrity in denied connectivity scenarios, buffering intelligence for transmission once links were re-established.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">Operational highlights</h3>
          <p>Across these engagements, MEAICON's defence infrastructure consistently delivered three capabilities that traditional IT architectures could not: capture-resistant security that survives physical loss of equipment, grid-independent operation in austere forward-deployed environments, and sovereign data sovereignty with no dependency on external cloud providers or foreign jurisdictions.</p>
          <p>Each deployment was tailored to the specific threat model and regulatory framework of the host nation, with hardware-enforced controls replacing policy-based controls wherever mission data was at stake. Post-quantum cryptography ensured that intercepted intelligence retained confidentiality well beyond current decryption horizons.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

